ticket.text:
Dispensing: Support limiting prescriptions shown to locations under session's visit location

The dispensing app has an Active Prescriptions and All Prescriptions tab, both containing a table showing prescriptions. The table can be configured to show a location filter, allowing the user to filter prescriptions for the selection locations.

We want to be able to further configure the location behavior, by introducing a `limitFilterOptionsBySessionVisitLocation` config, so that:

- if true, limits the location selections dropdown to only those under the ancestor visit location for the user’s session location.
- limit prescriptions rows shown to locations under user session’s visit location.

For example, suppose we have 2 hospitals. Within the system, both are “Visit Locations”. If I’m logged in to a (child) location under hospital A. I only want to see prescriptions form hospital A, and that the location filter to have location options from hospital A and not hospital B.

Implementation-wise, we’d be modifying `config-schema.ts` :

```
  locationBehavior: {
    locationColumn: {
      enabled: boolean;
    };
    locationFilter: {
      enabled: boolean;
      tag: string;
      associatedPharmacyLocationAttribute: string;
    };

    limitFilterOptionsBySessionVisitLocation: boolean; // new field here
  };
```
